   "text": "I read this as a rifamycin-type ansa macrolactam with the naphthoquinone fused to a phenoxazine ring. The phenoxazine carries a 2-(2-azabicyclo[2.2.1]heptan-2-yl)ethoxy group.\n\n**Core.**\n- The furanone has a quaternary carbon bearing a methyl group, the ring oxygen, the C=O and a wedged O\u2013CH=CH ansa bond.\n- The aromatic ring carries a methyl and an OH.\n- The quinone ring is fused to the phenoxazine, with the NH-amide on the ring carbon next to the quinone C=O.\n\n**Phenoxazine substituent.** The benzo ring bears O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013N. The nitrogen is N2 of an azabicyclo[2.2.1]heptane: it is bonded to one bridgehead carbon and to a CH2 that leads to the other bridgehead.\n\n**Ansa chain.** Starting from the vinyl ether, the chain runs:\n- O\u2013CH=CH (trans)\n- CH(OMe)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OAc)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OH)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH(OH)\n- CH(CH3)\n- CH=CH (trans)\n- CH=C(CH3) (cis)\n- C(=O)NH\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I worked out each centre from the wedges and hashes. The one-line summary:\n- The OMe is hashed.\n- The OAc and the two methyls at the OAc end are wedged or hashed as drawn.\n- The OH groups are hashed.\n- The methyl next to the diene is wedged.\n- The quaternary carbon has the hashed methyl and the wedged O-vinyl bond.\n\nI wrote the ring system in Kekul\u00e9 form to avoid aromaticity problems with the quinone carbonyls.\n\nSMILES: CO[C@H]1/C=C/O[C@@]2(C)OC3=C(C)C(O)=C4C(=C3C2=O)C5=NC6=CC=C(OCCN7CC8CCC7C8)C=C6OC5=C(NC(=O)/C(C)=C\\C=C\\[C@H](C)[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@H](OC(C)=O)[C@@H]1C)C4=O"
